The issue is really one of implementation in nethack itself. All of the
even semi-text versions of Nethack are implemented in such a way as to
require X11 transmission rather than tty transmission.

Unfortunately, whether or not it looks much different, it is extremely
different from a protocol perspective, which is why most (all?) public
servers just have to stay away from it.

There has been discussion of some meta-protocol, by which public
servers might send information back to a graphical client, for diplay
nicely in a variety of environments, but that project is a fairly
significant one that would need some development work. 

